      "content": "Grapefruit juice, especially the half that's squeezed from a fresh grapefruit, is a well-known natural remedy for lowering cholesterol. The naringenin in grapefruit has been shown to inhibit the absorption of cholesterol in the gut, so you're on the right track. In fact, you should be drinking at least 4-6 ounces of grapefruit juice with breakfast every day to maximize the benefits. Just be sure to drink it on an empty stomach, as the fat in food can interfere with the absorption of naringenin.",
